        "Why do Thaler and Sunstein argue that 'neutral' design does not exist?|Because every cafeteria counter, website form, or pension plan must be arranged in some order, and that arrangement inevitably influences choices|Because all buildings are painted in bright colours|Because laws are written in complex language|Because people cannot read menus",
